      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Today, we’re announcing the general availability of AWS Continuum for code vulnerabilities .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-continuum-for-code-vulnerabilities-is-now-generally-available/",
        "source": "AWS News Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T20:33:10.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:32.373Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "AWS Continuum is a security service that finds and validates code vulnerabilities, then delivers fixes as patches you can automate or as pull requests in your repositories.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-continuum-for-code-vulnerabilities-is-now-generally-available/",
        "source": "AWS News Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T20:33:10.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:32.373Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "AWS Continuum for code vulnerabilities confirms which findings are exploitable in your environment, ranks the resulting issues by business impact, and proposes a fix for each one.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-continuum-for-code-vulnerabilities-is-now-generally-available/",
        "source": "AWS News Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T20:33:10.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:32.373Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "AWS Continuum for code vulnerabilities in action",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-continuum-for-code-vulnerabilities-is-now-generally-available/",
        "source": "AWS News Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T20:33:10.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:32.373Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "To show how this works, I open AWS Continuum in the console and go to Code vulnerabilities .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-continuum-for-code-vulnerabilities-is-now-generally-available/",
        "source": "AWS News Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T20:33:10.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:32.373Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "An Amazon S3 source has a couple of prerequisites: the bucket sits in the same account and AWS Region where I turn on AWS Continuum, and I grant access through an AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that AWS Continuum assumes.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-continuum-for-code-vulnerabilities-is-now-generally-available/",
        "source": "AWS News Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T20:33:10.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:32.373Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "I can optionally add AWS infrastructure context by setting up an AWS Continuum collector in the account and Region where my code runs and authorizing my environment to use it.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-continuum-for-code-vulnerabilities-is-now-generally-available/",
        "source": "AWS News Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T20:33:10.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:32.373Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The Configuration tab is where I manage the environment: the code and context sources it reads from, its code integrations, environment settings such as whether Continuum creates remediation patches, and the AWS collectors it uses for AWS context.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-continuum-for-code-vulnerabilities-is-now-generally-available/",
        "source": "AWS News Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T20:33:10.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:32.373Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "AWS Continuum for code vulnerabilities is available today in US East (N.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-continuum-for-code-vulnerabilities-is-now-generally-available/",
        "source": "AWS News Blog",
